Vb2RiM1JwdTVBbUNPSVB1YlJiaGdQV253Z1hmb0hMX0JXUlhMYm5zMlVoazdHQXJ1NlVUQjJLeHUyWQ?oc=5","date":"2026-11-04","zh":"Healthpeak Properties (DOC) 在第三季財報電話會議上的講話"},{"title":"Healthpeak Properties: Potential Life Science Rebound Creates A Strong Re-Rating Setup","src":"Seeking Alpha","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxOZ3VjYURaLS1jS1F6WWdfUmlmUnJrQzdTUEhkQ1lOVDNtc3l5X3RkTlVla0JwVmk0NTZGRW05T1VpaHpqMEdBNDF6X1lJbGhxTDh2ZU4tNm1uZENLNG0ybDJHaWRpdjAyUGRuZjBPZ2NXRjByUzloQUk0cFVrdWZHUTBaQUswb2R1OWlrSG1tNTdBOFQ3N1dWSGpHMGY5cG9XWDh1MUF2MzZtdFpyUUhoYnJxRFBYM3JROEVQOVA4VVJQbHF0?oc=5","date":"2026-11-04","zh":"Healthpeak Properties：潛在的生命科學反彈創造了強勁的重新評級設置"},{"title":"Healthpeak Properties (DOC) Stock Shrugs Off Q3 Earnings Guidance Lift","src":"Simply Wall St","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-11-04","zh":"Healthpeak Properties (DOC) 股票不受第三季獲利指引提升的影響"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":5},{"name":"分析師評等","count":5},{"name":"AI 人工智慧","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-03","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/765880/000162828026005044/peak-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Healthpeak Properties, Inc. is a Standard & Poor's (\"S&P\") 500 company that owns, operates, and develops high-quality real estate focused on healthcare discovery and delivery in the United States (\"U.S.\"). Our company was originally founded in 1985. We are organized as an umbrella partnership REIT (\"UPREIT\"). We hold substantially all of our assets and conduct our operations through our operating subsidiary, Healthpeak OP, a consolidated subsidiary of which we are the managing member. We are a Maryland corporation and qualify as a self-administered REIT. We are headquartered in Denver, Colorado, with additional corporate offices in California, Tennessee, Wisconsin, and Massachusetts and property management offices in several locations throughout the U.S.","zh":null},{"en":"We have a diversified portfolio of high-quality healthcare properties across three core asset classes of outpatient medical, lab, and senior housing real estate. Under the outpatient medical and lab segments, we own, operate, and develop outpatient medical buildings, hospitals, and lab buildings. Under the senior housing segment, our properties are operated through RIDEA structures. We have other non-reportable segments that are comprised primarily of: (i) loans receivable, (ii) a preferred equity investment, and (iii) three other properties. These non-reportable segments have been presented on a combined basis herein.","zh":null},{"en":"On March 1, 2024 (the \"Closing Date\"), we completed our merger with Physicians Realty Trust (the \"Merger\"). Subsequent to the Closing Date, the \"Combined Company\" means Healthpeak and its subsidiaries. As a result of the Merger, we acquired 299 outpatient medical buildings. See Note 3 to the Consolidated Financial Statements for additional information.","zh":null}],"markets":[{"en":"Our outpatient medical segment includes outpatient medical buildings and hospitals. Outpatient medical buildings typically contain physicians' offices and examination rooms, and may also include pharmacies, hospital ancillary service space, and outpatient services such as diagnostic centers, rehabilitation clinics, and day-surgery operating rooms. While these facilities have certain similarities to commercial office buildings, they require additional plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems to accommodate multiple exam rooms that may require sinks in every room and specialized equipment such as x-ray machines and MRIs. Outpatient medical buildings are often built to accommodate higher structural loads for such specialized equipment and may contain vaults or other unique construction. Our outpatient medical buildings are typically multi-tenant properties leased to healthcare providers","zh":null},{"en":"The following table provides information about our most significant outpatient medical tenant concentration for the year ended December 31, 2025:","zh":null}],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"Investing in real estate serving the healthcare industry is highly competitive. We face competition from other REITs, investment companies, pension funds, private equity investors, sovereign funds, healthcare operators, lenders, developers, and other institutional investors, some of whom may have greater flexibility (e.g., non-REIT competitors), greater resources, and lower costs of capital than we do. Increased competition and resulting capitalization rate compression, as well as the impacts of elevated interest rates, make it more challenging for us to identify and successfully capitalize on opportunities that meet our objectives. Our ability to compete may also be impacted by global, national, and local economic trends, availability of investment alternatives, availability and cost of capital, construction and renovation costs, existing laws and regulations, new legislation, and popul","zh":null},{"en":"Income from our investments depends on our tenants' and operators' ability to compete with other companies on multiple levels, including: (i) the quality of care provided, (ii) reputation, (iii) success of product or drug development, (iv) price, (v) the range of services offered, (vi) the physical appearance of a property, (vii) alternatives for healthcare delivery, (viii) the supply of competing properties, (ix) physicians, (x) staff, (xi) referral sources, (xii) location, (xiii) the size and demographics of the population in surrounding areas, and (xiv) the financial condition of our tenants and operators. For a discussion of the risks associated with competitive conditions affecting our business, see \"Item 1A, Risk Factors\" in this report.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Outpatient Medical","val":1273505000,"zh":"Outpatient Medical"},{"name":"Lab","val":860020000,"zh":"Lab"},{"name":"Senior Housing","val":603989000,"zh":"Senior Housing"}],"total":2822512000}},"peers":["SBRA","LTC","STAG","DEA","WPC"]}}